# when-block: the block form of when...otherwise, closed by stop when.
create a variable called x as an integer with a value of 0
create a variable called one as an integer with a value of 1

repeat while the variable x is less than 6:
	add the variable one to the variable x
	when the variable x is equal to 2:
		write out the string "two"
		write out the string "even"
	otherwise:
		write out the variable x
		when the variable x is greater than 4 write out the string "big"
	stop when.
stop repeating.

when the variable x is equal to 6:
	write out the string "finished"
stop when.